# .ai-taskrc - example config for ai-task.sh
#
# This file is sourced as a plain bash script, so any shell syntax works,
# but plain variable assignments (no `export` needed) are the norm.
#
# Copy this to one of (name it either `ai-task.conf` or `.ai-taskrc` - both
# names are checked at both scopes):
#   $HOME/.config/ai-task/ai-task.conf   - your global defaults
#   $HOME/.ai-taskrc                     - your global defaults (rc-style)
#   $(pwd)/ai-task.conf                  - project-local overrides (e.g. repo root)
#   $(pwd)/.ai-taskrc                    - project-local overrides (rc-style)
# All present ones are loaded, home scope first, then cwd on top. An env
# var you set for this specific invocation always wins over any of them.

# Required - no hardcoded default. If unset here, you'll be prompted once
# and the answer gets appended to this file (or created fresh if neither
# config file exists yet).
#AITASK_TEAM="MYTEAM"

# Optional overrides - shown here with the script's own hardcoded defaults.
# Uncomment and edit as needed.

# AITASK_LABEL="aitask"
# AITASK_ASSIGNEE="self"
# AITASK_STATE="unstarted"
# AITASK_CYCLE="active"
# AITASK_SORT="priority"
# AITASK_PRIORITY=""                # 1-4, unset = no filter
# AITASK_IN_PROGRESS_STATE="In Progress"
# AITASK_BLOCKED_STATE="Blocked"
# AITASK_PERMISSION_MODE="auto"     # claude --permission-mode value (claude only)

# Which agent CLI to launch: "claude" (default) or "opencode".
# AITASK_AGENT_TYPE="claude"

# Model for the launched session - format depends on AITASK_AGENT_TYPE (see
# README.md "Agent backends" / "Looking up model names"):
#   claude:   an alias ("sonnet", "opus", "fable") or full model name, e.g.
#             claude-sonnet-5 - run `claude` and type `/model` for the
#             current live list rather than trusting a hardcoded one here.
#   opencode: "provider/model", e.g. anthropic/claude-sonnet-5 - run
#             `opencode models` to list what's available to your account.
# AITASK_MODEL="claude-sonnet-5"

# Settings/config JSON file for the selected agent, merged in at runtime
# (claude: passed to --settings; opencode: merged into the generated
# OPENCODE_CONFIG alongside the required opencode-sandbox plugin entry).
# Trusted input - only point this at a file you wrote or trust.
# AITASK_AGENT_SETTINGS="$HOME/.config/ai-task/my-agent-settings.json"

# Where new worktrees get created. Defaults to
# $HOME/.local/ai-task/worktrees/<repo-name> - a location this script owns
# and controls, independent of any particular terminal app/IDE. If you'd
# rather share worktrees with another tool's layout instead (so that tool
# can also see/open them), point this at its convention. See README.md for
# a list of what a few common tools use.
# AITASK_WORKTREE_ROOT="$HOME/.local/ai-task/worktrees/my-repo"

# AWS ReadOnly mode: pre-auth read-only AWS credentials + AWS-specific
# prompt and sandbox additions (see the aws-preauth command). ON BY
# DEFAULT. Set false for a repo with no AWS/terraform component - the
# script works fine without it, it just won't touch AWS at all.
# AITASK_AWS_READONLY="false"

# Comma-separated extra hosts for the sandbox network allowlist, on top of
# the built-in defaults (github.com, linear.app, + AWS hosts if AWS
# ReadOnly mode is on).
# AITASK_ALLOWED_HOSTS="registry.npmjs.org,pypi.org"

# A custom prompt template file (see ai-task.sh --help for the placeholder
# tokens it supports) and/or extra literal text appended to whichever
# prompt is used.
# AITASK_PROMPT_FILE="$HOME/.config/ai-task/my-prompt.txt"
# AITASK_PROMPT_EXTRA="Prefer small, incremental commits."
